{
  "id": "COMPOUND:24782 - PROTEIN:6305",
  "verbalization": "Melitensin is implicated in targeting the CD70 antigen, which in turn is a target of multiple compounds, including Spruceanol and Capensinidin. These compounds are all linked to the Vacuolar ATP synthase subunit S1, suggesting a potential pathway where Melitensin may exert its effects through a shared mechanism involving the CD70 antigen. The evidence points to a possible dependency on the CD70 antigen as a critical node in the interaction network, with Melitensin potentially acting through this antigen to influence the activity of the Vacuolar ATP synthase subunit S1. The consistent targeting of CD70 antigen by Melitensin and its downstream effect on the Vacuolar ATP synthase subunit S1 implies a functional link that could be further explored to understand the broader implications of this interaction.",
